<!--
  SpotBugs/FindSecBugs exclusions. Keep this list short.
  Every entry names the bug pattern, the class and, where possible, the method; carries a comment with the
  justification; and is approved in review by a maintainer with the security role (BUILD_PLAN section 12).
  Prefer @SuppressFBWarnings(value = "...", justification = "...") at the narrowest scope where the annotation
  dependency's license allows it (spotbugs-annotations is LGPL-2.1, not on the allow-list, hence this file).
-->
<FindBugsFilter
    xmlns="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/spotbugs/spotbugs/3.1.0/spotbugs/etc/findbugsfilter.xsd">
  <!--
    SERVLET_HEADER (FindSecBugs, Low) in RequestIdFilter.doFilterInternal: the client-supplied X-Request-Id is used
    only after it matches a 1-64 character [A-Za-z0-9._-] allow-list (RequestIdFilter.resolve); anything else is
    replaced by a random UUID. Covered by RequestIdFilterTest. Added in PR 12; needs security-role approval.
    An annotation is not used because spotbugs-annotations is LGPL-2.1, outside security/licenses-allowed.txt.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Class name="io.trailkeep.shared.observability.RequestIdFilter"/>
    <Method name="doFilterInternal"/>
    <Bug pattern="SERVLET_HEADER"/>
  </Match>
  <!--
    FindSecBugs SPRING_ENDPOINT marks every controller for review; it reports no defect. Each class below was reviewed:
    DashboardController (PR 9, WP-05): GET only, renders the signed-in user's own display name, behind login.
    SessionController (PR 9, WP-05): POST only, CSRF-protected, behind login, changes only the session's idle clock.
    TeamAdminController (WP-09): behind login, CSRF on every POST; TeamAdminService refuses anyone but a System Admin,
    rebuilding permissions from the database per request. Covered by TeamAdminControllerIT (403, 404, 422, CSRF).
    CaseConfigController (WP-10): behind login, CSRF on every POST; CaseConfigService refuses anyone but a Compliance
    Admin, rebuilding permissions from the database per request. Covered by CaseConfigControllerIT (403, 404, 422,
    CSRF). Approved in the security-reviewer role on #22.
    CaseController (WP-11): GET only, behind login; CaseService reads through the person's CaseScope, rebuilding
    permissions from the database per request, and answers 404 for a malformed, absent or unreadable case number.
    Covered by CaseControllerIT. Approved in the security-reviewer role on #39.
    WP-11 part 2b adds POST /cases (CSRF, behind login): CaseService checks CREATE against the matrix and every
    reference before writing; form values are echoed only through th:value/th:text. Covered by CaseCreateControllerIT
    (403 for Reader and System Admin, CSRF, 422). POST approved in the security-reviewer role on #41.
    WP-13 part 2 adds POST /cases/{number}/comments (CSRF, behind login): CaseCommentService reads through the
    person's CaseScope (404 if unreadable) and checks COMMENT against the matrix (403), rebuilding permissions from
    the database per request, before the body is looked at (422). The body is echoed only through th:text and shown
    only as SafeHtml through tk:safe. Covered by CaseCommentControllerIT (Analyst allowed, Reader 403, unreadable
    404, CSRF 403, 422). Approved in the security-reviewer role on #52.
    WP-13 part 3 adds POST /cases/{number}/comments/pin and /unpin (CSRF, behind login): CaseCommentService reads
    through the person's CaseScope (404 if unreadable) and checks PIN against the matrix (403), rebuilding
    permissions from the database per request, before the submitted comment id is looked at; an id naming no comment
    of that case, read through the same scope, is 422, and the database's composite key refuses a pin on another
    case's comment. The id is parsed leniently, so a malformed one cannot answer before those checks, and the redirect
    carries only the parsed number. Covered by CaseCommentPinControllerIT (Analyst allowed, Reader 403, unreadable
    404, CSRF 403, 422). Approved in the security-reviewer role on #53.
    WP-14 part 3 adds POST /cases/{number}/attachments (multipart, CSRF, behind login): CaseAttachmentService reads
    through the person's CaseScope (404 if unreadable) and checks COMMENT ("add comment / attachment") against the
    matrix (403), rebuilding permissions from the database per request, before the file is read; then UploadIntake
    validates (422) and scans it (503 if the scanner gives no verdict) with no transaction open, and only then is
    anything stored. The browser's file name never forms a path (the temp file is named by Files.createTempFile), is
    never logged, is audited only as an HMAC, and is echoed only through th:text. Covered by CaseAttachmentUploadIT
    and ExternalScanningUploadIT (Analyst allowed, Reader 403, unreadable 404, CSRF 403, 422 per reason, 503 with
    nothing stored, temp file gone). Approved in the security-reviewer role on #58.
    CaseEditController (WP-12): GET and POST /cases/{number}/edit, behind login, CSRF on the POST. Every request first
    calls CaseService.editable, which reads through the person's CaseScope (404 if unreadable) and checks EDIT against
    the matrix (403), rebuilding permissions from the database per request; the save is checked again in the service
    against the submitted version (409). Form values are echoed only through th:value/th:text. Covered by
    CaseEditControllerIT (Analyst allowed, Reader 403, unreadable 404, CSRF 403, stale version 409). Approved in the
    security-reviewer role on #49.
    CaseAssignmentController (WP-12 part 2): GET and POST /cases/{number}/reassign, /restrict and /unrestrict, behind
    login, CSRF on every POST. Every request first calls CaseAssignmentService, which reads through the person's
    CaseScope (404 if unreadable) and checks REASSIGN, RESTRICT or UNRESTRICT against the matrix (403), rebuilding
    permissions from the database per request, before input (422) or version (409). Ids are parsed leniently, so a
    malformed one cannot answer before those checks. Values are echoed only through th:value/th:text. Covered by
    CaseAssignmentControllerIT (allowed role, nearest disallowed role 403, unreadable 404, CSRF 403, stale 409).
    Approved in the security-reviewer role on #50.
    CaseAttachmentController (WP-14 part 4): GET /cases/{number}/attachments/{id} (download), and GET and POST
    /cases/{number}/attachments/{id}/release, behind login, CSRF on the POST. CaseAttachmentService first reads through
    the person's CaseScope (404 if unreadable), checks DOWNLOAD_ATTACHMENT or RELEASE_QUARANTINE against the matrix
    (403), rebuilding permissions from the database per request, and finds the id only among that case's attachments
    through the same scope (404 for another case's id, so ids cannot be probed); a quarantined file is 403 and never
    read. The id is parsed leniently, so a malformed one cannot answer before those checks. The download carries
    Content-Disposition: attachment built by AttachmentDisposition (ASCII fallback with every non-printable, quote,
    backslash and percent replaced, and an RFC 5987 percent-encoded filename*, so no CR, LF or quote from the name
    reaches the header), nosniff and Cache-Control: private, no-store; the release reason is echoed only through
    th:text and audited only as an HMAC. Covered by CaseAttachmentDownloadIT, CaseAttachmentReleaseIT and
    AttachmentDispositionTest (allowed role, nearest disallowed role 403, unreadable 404, another case's id 404,
    CSRF 403, 422, hostile names). Approved in the security-reviewer role on #59.
    CaseListController (WP-15 part 1a): GET /cases only, behind login, no state change. CaseListQuery.parse reads the
    query string into the allow-listed CaseSort, a direction and a page number (422 for anything else, an unknown sort
    column included); CaseListService counts and lists only through the person's CaseScope, rebuilding permissions
    from the database per request, so unreadable cases are absent from rows and counts. The HX-Trigger header is used
    only if it matches a fixed id pattern, and every value is echoed through th:text or built from enum names and
    numbers by CaseListQuery.toQueryString. Covered by CaseListControllerIT and CaseListServiceIT. Approved in
    the security-reviewer role on #62.
    UserAdminController (#31): behind login, CSRF on every POST; UserAdminService refuses anyone but a System Admin,
    rebuilding permissions from the database per request, and refuses disabling oneself. Covered by
    UserAdminControllerIT (System Admin allowed, Compliance Admin 403, unknown user 404, self 422, CSRF, anonymous),
    UserAdminServiceIT and SharedSessionsIT (CSRF-protected POST through a real login). Approved in the
    security-reviewer role on #63.
    SavedViewController (WP-15 part 3): behind login; POST /cases/views and POST /cases/views/{id}/delete carry CSRF
    (403 without). The posted query is read back through CaseListQuery.parse (422 for any value no form offers) and
    stored in its canonical form, so a view holds only allow-listed criteria and applies through the person's
    CaseScope like any URL; the redirect after a save is the fixed path /cases plus that canonical query string. Every
    lookup and delete carries the owner's id, so another person's view or an unknown id is 404, never 403. The name
    is echoed only through th:text and audited by name only. Covered by SavedViewServiceIT and
    SavedViewControllerIT. Approved in the security-reviewer role on #78.
    CaseHistoryController (WP-16): GET /cases/{number}/history only, behind login, no state change except the audit
    event of reading a restricted case. The kind is read into the allow-listed HistoryKind and the page into a positive
    integer (422 for anything else); CaseHistoryService finds the case through the person's CaseScope (404 if
    unreadable), rebuilding permissions from the database per request, and reads the events through AuditTrailService
    with the same scope. Every value is echoed through th:text, and a redacted field reaches the page as "set" or
    "changed" only. Covered by CaseHistoryControllerIT, CaseHistoryAccessibilityIT and RestrictedViewAuditIT.
    Approved in the security-reviewer role on #87.
    CaseExportController (WP-15 part 4): GET /cases/export.csv, behind login; the only write is the CASES_EXPORTED
    audit row. CaseListQuery.parse reads the list's own query string (422 for any value no form offers); the export
    reads through the person's CaseScope with the list's WHERE, so unreadable cases are absent; details=true is
    honoured only for a Manager of the case's team or a Compliance Admin and silently redacted otherwise; a filter
    over app.export.max-rows is 422; selected ids are parsed case numbers (at most 100) under the same WHERE. The
    Content-Disposition file name is "cases-" plus a formatted timestamp, never
    user input; every cell is quoted and defused against formula injection by CsvFormat. Covered by CsvFormatTest,
    CaseExportIT, OracleCaseExportIT and CaseExportControllerIT. Approved in the security-reviewer role on #84.
    AlertController (WP-17 part c): behind login; GET /alerts lists only the signed-in person's alerts (the page is
    parsed to a number and clamped, nothing else is read) and marks nothing read; POST /alerts/{id}/read and POST
    /alerts/{id}/delete carry CSRF (403 without) and every lookup carries the person's own id, so another person's
    alert or an unknown id is 404, never 403. The redirect is the fixed path /alerts plus a parsed page number. Alert
    text and links are written only by NotificationService (a link is a single-slash path inside the application)
    and echoed through th:text and @{...}. Covered by UserAlertServiceIT, AlertControllerIT and AlertsAccessibilityIT.
    Needs security-reviewer approval.
    Approved in the security-reviewer role on #20. Listed by class, never by pattern alone, so each new controller
    is reviewed the same way.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Bug pattern="SPRING_ENDPOINT"/>
    <Or>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.DashboardController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.SessionController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.TeamAdminController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.UserAdminController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseConfigController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseEditController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseAssignmentController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseAttachmentController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseListController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.SavedViewController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseHistoryController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseExportController"/>
      <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.AlertController"/>
    </Or>
  </Match>
  <!--
    FindSecBugs SERVLET_HEADER: these read htmx's own request headers as rendering hints, never as a trust decision.
    HX-Request only selects a fragment or an HX-Redirect instead of a full page; authorization is unchanged.
    HX-Current-URL is reduced to a same-origin absolute path (no scheme, host or "//"), so the HX-Redirect built from
    it cannot leave the application (HtmxAwareResponses.currentPath, tested in WebShellIT).
    CaseListController.list (WP-15 part 1a): HX-Request selects the results fragment; HX-Trigger is used only if it
    matches the fixed pattern tk-(sort-[a-z]+|page-(previous|next)) and then only names which element gets
    data-tk-focus; anything else is dropped (tested in CaseListControllerIT with a hostile value). Approved in
    the security-reviewer role on #62.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Bug pattern="SERVLET_HEADER"/>
    <Or>
      <And>
        <Class name="io.trailkeep.security.HtmxAwareResponses"/>
        <Or>
          <Method name="isHtmx"/>
          <Method name="currentPath"/>
        </Or>
      </And>
      <And>
        <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.ErrorAdvice"/>
        <Method name="domain"/>
      </And>
      <And>
        <Class name="io.trailkeep.web.CaseListController"/>
        <Method name="list"/>
      </And>
    </Or>
  </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
